hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3961","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wrongdoing is of three kinds: a wrongdoing that Allah will not forgive, a wrongdoing that He will forgive, and a wrongdoing that He will not leave. As for the wrongdoing that Allah will not forgive, it is shirk; Allah Almighty said: Indeed, shirk is a tremendous wrongdoing. As for the wrongdoing that He will forgive, it is the servants wronging their own souls in what is between them and their Lord. And as for the wrongdoing that Allah will not leave, it is the servants wronging one another, until He exacts retribution for them from one another."
"3962","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A mortgaged riding animal may be ridden in return for spending on it, and a mortgaged milch animal's milk may be drunk in return for spending on it; and the one who rides and drinks is the one responsible for its upkeep."
